Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/os/StrictMode.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
ADR-0039 step c2d3: a VM policy that detects unsafe intent launches registers no callback with the activity manager.

Why: setVmPolicy registers StrictMode's callback for unsafe intent launches with the activity manager whenever the
policy detects them, as enableDefaults' detectAll does for target SDK 31 and later. Minato has no activity manager
(ActivityManager.getService answers null) and framework.jar leaves IActivityManager out, so the call ended the app
with NoClassDefFoundError. The activity manager calls it back when the app starts an intent that its rules find
unsafe; Minato's starts do not go through an activity manager, so no call would come.

--- a/core/java/android/os/StrictMode.java
+++ b/core/java/android/os/StrictMode.java
@@ -2153,14 +2153,6 @@
     private static volatile UnsafeIntentStrictModeCallback sUnsafeIntentCallback;
 
     private static void registerIntentMatchingRestrictionCallback() {
-        if (sUnsafeIntentCallback == null) {
-            sUnsafeIntentCallback = new UnsafeIntentStrictModeCallback();
-            try {
-                ActivityManager.getService().registerStrictModeCallback(sUnsafeIntentCallback);
-            } catch (RemoteException e) {
-                // system_server should not throw
-            }
-        }
     }
 
     /** Gets the current VM policy. */
